  "summary": "temporalStorageForm (@objectstack/core) now reads a finite number on a `date` field as the UTC calendar day of new Date(value): the same conversion a Date takes, so a number and its Date always agree. NaN, ±Infinity and numbers past the Date range come back unchanged. driver-sql (toDateOnly / temporalFilterValue), driver-memory (coerceTemporalValue) and the engine's per-aggregation filter / having already call this rule, so there is no driver source change. One REST request that answered memory 0, SQLite 6 of 6 and PostgreSQL DATABASE_ERROR/500 now answers the date's own count on all three (e.g. $gt 1769940000000 → 1 row), and where = per-aggregation filter = having on every cell. Every datetime, time and non-number date cell is byte-identical base → head. Stop valve: ADR-0053 states no requirement that a date comparand be a calendar-day string, so the read direction was taken. Draft PR #20224; the card had assignee os-sales on arrival, and PR #20224 now carries the same assignee.",
  "tests": "Commits: the fix ba5c0de774; tests 6cb41f4200; changesets 4c8b92e022; merge of main 16aedcab30; final 1c8c5ce756 (types the three new pins' query options, test files only). Pins: core temporal-storage-form.test.ts 72 passed (file unchanged since 4c8b92e022); at 1c8c5ce756 driver-sql sql-driver-20203-epoch-ms-date-comparand.test.ts on SQLite + live PostgreSQL 16.13 (TZ=America/New_York, server Asia/Shanghai) 46 passed | 1 skipped (MySQL declared unprovisioned); driver-memory memory-20203-epoch-ms-date-comparand.test.ts 23 passed; rest data-query-epoch-ms-date-comparand.test.ts 18 passed. Whole suites at 16aedcab30, after merging main 4df101c383 and rebuilding the closure (vitest run, no --project, so both local and repo projects): core 57 files / 1488 passed; driver-memory 55 / 1351 passed; driver-sql with live PostgreSQL 197 passed, 3 skipped files / 3852 passed, 87 skipped (reporter: sqlite RAN, live postgres RAN, live mysql NOT RUN); objectql 319 / 5767 passed; rest (includes every query-route test) 201 / 3582 passed, 1 skipped. Typecheck: core at 16aedcab30, driver-memory / driver-sql / rest at 1c8c5ce756, exit 0 each; every new/changed test file is in a compiled program by --listFiles (tsconfig.json for the drivers, tsconfig.test.json for core and rest); test-typecheck ledgers unchanged (core 4 held, rest 0). Ablation at 4c8b92e022 (fix committed first; ablation-replace wrap mode with EXIT/INT/TERM restore on the absolute path): anchor \"const instant = typeof value === 'number' && Number.isFinite(value) ? new Date(value) : value;\" x1 → x0, blob 61a6c0861a → 2a9bd5d997; core rebuilt; ablation-dist-preflight --absent exit 0 (marker gone from dist). Mutated: core 13 failed / 59 passed; memory 12 failed / 11 passed (the empty-object rows); driver-sql 35 failed / 11 passed / 1 skipped (SQLite empties green, PG empties red: the 500 came back); rest 17 failed / 1 passed (the min(datetime) control). Restored by the tool: blob == HEAD 61a6c0861a, git diff HEAD empty, whole-tree git status --porcelain empty; core rebuilt; preflight marker present exit 0; pins 72 / 23 / 46+1 skipped / 18 passed. Reverse-verification direction observed: turned red (the ordinary direction).",
