    "class: a · the date rule's Date conversion (`${y}-${m}-${d}` from getUTCFullYear, in core temporal-storage-form.ts, formerly each driver's copy) spells a year outside 1000..9999 unpadded, so the text no longer orders or parses as a YYYY-MM-DD day. Measured at head, same six-row fixture, REST number and in-process Date agree: year 999 → memory/SQLite $gt 0 / $lt 6 (PG 6 / 0, correct); year 10000 → memory/SQLite 6 / 0 (PG 0 / 6, correct); year -1 → PG DATABASE_ERROR / 500. Reachable in-process by a Date before this PR, and by a REST number after it. See open_questions[0]. · dedupe words: date rule year below 1000 unpadded · calendar day year outside 4 digits text order · toDateOnly getUTCFullYear padding",
